# Key Points for Revision

- JVM = Class Loader + Runtime Data Areas + Execution Engine.
- Heap stores Objects.
- Stack stores Method Calls and Local Variables.
- Metaspace stores Class Metadata.
- Code Cache stores JIT compiled native code.
- Heap is Shared.
- Stack is Thread Specific.
- JIT improves performance.
- Garbage Collector works mainly on Heap.
- Java 8 replaced PermGen with Metaspace.

---

# One-Line Summary

JVM loads classes through the Class Loader, stores execution data in Runtime Data Areas (Heap, Stack, Metaspace, Code Cache), 
and executes bytecode using the Execution Engine consisting of Interpreter, JIT Compiler, and Garbage Collector.
